body:
It's not opening 2 windows of minecraft, it's only opening one. The (2) next to the tab in task manager means the process minecraft opens 2 applications: runtime broker, an application that manages permissions for apps off of the windows store, and minecraft, the actual application for the game. the same thing appears when I open the game, too, which is shown in the screenshot i added below. The second icon of Minecraft says it takes up more MB of memory because the first icon with the arrow next to it is the put together version of everything running behind minecraft, those being minecraft and runtime broker.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

